details:
(a) the number of remote villages in Jammu and Kashmir that still lack basic 4G or 5G mobile connectivity;
(b) the current status of optical fibre cable installation under the BharatNet project in rural blocks of the Union Territory; and
(c) the regulatory steps taken to minimize frequent internet disruptions impacting local businesses and students?

(a) whether Government has any comprehensive plan to develop and promote the unexplored tourist destinations of Kupwara district, including Lolab Valley, Bangus Valley, Keran and Machil at the national and international levels;
(b) the details of infrastructure projects, promotional initiatives and budgetary allocations for border and eco-tourism in these areas;
(c) the measures taken to provide tourist amenities, including roads, homestays, accommodation and mobile connectivity; and
(d) the number of local youth from Kupwara trained or employed under tourism-related skill development schemes during the last three years?

(a) the total funds sanctioned for constructing all-weather tunnels to connect seasonally isolated border regions like Gurez, Tangdhar and Marwah-Warwan;
(b) the current status of these projects and their definitive completion deadlines; and
(c) the interim emergency communication and healthcare infrastructure deployed by the Centre to support these populations during complete winter cut-offs?

(a) whether Government has assessed the infrastructure gaps in Government schools in Jammu & Kashmir, particularly the shortage of classrooms, playgrounds, science and computer laboratories, vocational education facilities and teaching staff;
(b) the steps taken to address these deficiencies and improve the quality of school education in the Union Territory; and
(c) the total Central funds released and utilised during the last three years for strengthening school infrastructure in Jammu & Kashmir under various Centrally Sponsored Schemes?

(a) the district-wise area covered under micro-irrigation in Jammu and Kashmir under the Per Drop More Crop component of PMKSY;
(b) whether Government has taken any special measures to support farmers affected by rainfall deficit, drying springs and irrigation shortages in the Union Territory;
(c) whether Government proposes to implement a climate-resilient agriculture and water conservation plan for Jammu and Kashmir and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the timeline to finish pending lift-irrigation schemes in the Kandi areas of the Jammu and Kashmir?

(a) the total area of traditional apple and walnut orchards converted into high-density plantations in Jammu and Kashmir under the Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH);
(b) the present rate of Government subsidy and the quantum of bank finance available to orchardists for establishing high-density orchards; and 
(c) the measures taken to ensure the availability of elite rootstocks and to protect apple growers from recurring losses due to unseasonal dry spells and climate change?

(a) whether Government's recent diplomatic engagements in West Asia are consistent with India's long-standing policy of non-alignment/strategic autonomy and balanced relations with all the countries in the region;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of its policy on India's energy security, regional connectivity and bilateral relations with neighbouring nations; and
(c) the steps being taken to uphold India's traditional non-aligned foreign policy while protecting its strategic, economic and diplomatic interests in West Asia?

(a) whether any comprehensive survey has been conducted to ascertain the root causes of drug addiction in Jammu & Kashmir;
(b) the quantity of narcotics seized in the UT over the last five years, details thereof; and
(c) the programmes for prevention, treatment and rehabilitation, details thereof?

(a) the reasons why the construction of the Akhal and Tangchatter bridges (Ganderbal), started in 2010, was halted in 2016 and remains pending despite being sanctioned as "languishing projects" in 2018;
(b) the status of the Pir Ki Gali Tunnel project and whether a definitive construction timeline has been established;
(c) reasons as to why several rural road projects, such as the Ramnagar to Chatrari and Mantalai to Dudu roads, have failed to meet their completion targets; and
(d) whether Government is investigating "administrative apathy" as a cause for these decade-long delays?

(a) the reason for major urban infrastructure works in Handwara have seen a lack of administrative input;
(b) the details of funds released and utilized under the Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) for drainage and waste management in Handwara town over the last two years; and
(c) the timeline for the completion of the indoor sports stadium in Handwara, a central project aimed at youth engagement that has faced multiple delays?

(a) the specific technical and financial parameters used to declare the 34-km Sopore–Kupwara Rail Link as "infeasible" in February, 2026;
(b) whether Government has considered the strategic and security importance of extending the rail network to a frontier district like Kupwara before dropping the project;
(c) whether any alternative survey is being conducted for a modified route to make the project viable; and
(d) the total expenditure already incurred on the preliminary surveys and land identification for this project since its initial announcement?

(a) the details of assessment of wind energy potential in Jammu & Kashmir; 
(b) the current status of NHPC wind project established in Reasi in 2012; and 
(c) the new wind energy projects planned or under implementation to generate electricity in the Union Territory?

(a) whether Khelo India Excellence Centre for Winter Games, announced in 2021 and inaugurated in 2022 at Gulmarg during the 2nd Khelo India Winter Games, remains non-existent on the ground with no visible progress;
(b) the reasons for this delay, current status of land acquisition, funding, infrastructure approvals along with a revised timeline for completion; and
(c) how the absence of this centre has increased training costs and challenges for winter athletes and the measures being taken to operationalize it at the earliest?

(a) the present status of the Detailed Project Report (DPR) for the proposed Sadhna Tunnel on the Kupwara–Karnah road and the reasons for delay in its finalization;
(b) the number of fatalities on Sadhna Pass due to avalanches and accidents during the last three years;
(c) whether funds have been earmarked under PM DevINE or any other Central scheme for 2026–27; and
(d) the timeline for laying the foundation stone to ensure all-weather connectivity to Karnah?

(a) whether Government is aware of the severe livelihood crisis faced by traditional stone carvers (sang taraash) of Sanderkoot in Bandipora, Jammu and Kashmir, following the mining ban imposed in 2019 which has halted access to essential devere stone and endangered a centuries-old cultural craft;
(b) the number of families affected, whether rehabilitation, financial assistance or skill-development measures have been provided; and
(c) whether Government proposes to introduce a sustainable and regulated mining policy or other remedial steps to safeguard artisans’ livelihoods and preserve this traditional heritage?

(a) whether Government proposes to include Bungus Valley, one of the most scenic and famous tourist destinations of North Kashmir, under the National Ropeways Development Programme being implemented in collaboration with NHLML;
(b) whether Government has conducted any feasibility study or DPR has been prepared for establishing a ropeway to Bungus Valley to improve connectivity to this area, promote sustainable tourism, generate employment for local youth and boost the regional economy; and
(c) whether Government intends to take immediate steps to explore and approve such a project?

(a) whether Government is aware that there is currently no direct all-weather road connecting Machil and Tangdhar via Keran, which significantly affects civilian movement, trade and strategic access in this border area of Kupwara district;
(b) whether any surveys, DPRs or proposals have been prepared for constructing or upgrading this crucial road, including timelines for completion, pending approvals and funding allocations; and
(c) the steps Government is taking to ensure year-round connectivity and improve infrastructure for the people and border security forces in this region?

(a) whether Government is aware that despite crores of rupees being spent under Jal Jeevan Mission and other water supply schemes, people in various parts of J and K, particularly in Rajwar, Handwara, still suffer for even a single drop of potable drinking water;
(b) the reasons for this persistent crisis despite the sanctioning of thousands of water supply schemes;
(c) whether any third-party audit has been conducted to assess ground water-level functionality of schemes and household tap connections; and
(d) measures proposed to ensure assured, regular and sustainable drinking water supply to affected areas?

(a) whether Government has conducted any recent assessment regarding the number of educated unemployed youth in the Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir;
(b) the latest unemployment rate in the Union Territory, as compared to the national average; and
(c) whether Government is aware that prolonged unemployment among youth in the Union Territory is contributing to serious social problems, including drug abuse and crime and whether Government proposes to introduce a special, region-specific employment package aimed exclusively at generating sustainable job opportunities for unemployed youth of the Union Territory?

(a) despite the flagship “Har Ghar Nal, Har Ghar Jal” scheme promising piped drinking water to every household, several areas of Jammu and Kashmir still lack reliable supply, the reasons thereof;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the status of water supply projects in remote areas such as Rajwar, Handwara where residents reportedly continue to suffer for even a drop of water despite crores spent on Jal Jeevan Mission works; and
(c) reasons that can explain delays, poor quality and non-functional infrastructure, and the concrete steps and timelines to ensure water supply to these underserved areas?

(a) whether Government is aware that inhabitants of villages Kangan, Babhar, Sona Samil and Arabal in District Pulwama, Jammu and Kashmir, have strongly objected to the proposed railway track alignment, citing serious risks to residential habitations, fertile horticultural land and environmental safety;
(b) whether these objections and representations have been examined by the competent authorities;
(c) whether any fresh technical, environmental or social impact review has been proposed; and
(d) whether Government will consider a safer alternative alignment while ensuring protection of livelihoods and public safety?

(a) whether NHPC currently operates six hydropower projects in J&K Salal (690 MW), Uri-I (480 MW), Dulhasti (390 MW), Sewa-II (120 MW), Uri-II (240 MW) and Kishanganga (330 MW) with a total capacity of 2,250 MW;
(b) the present status in the 850 MW Ratle and 1,000 MW Pakal Dul joint venture hydroelectric projects;
(c) whether NHPC’s projects are being transferred to the UT Government after having recovered the total cost and profit since long; and
(d) whether BHEL’s thermal power project initiated at Nichhama Rajwar Handwara was abandoned in 1989 due to militancy and whether Government plans to revive it, if so, by when?

(a) whether Government has taken any step regarding the long-pending demand for construction of the Bandipora-Lolab road and four-laning of Sangrama-Chowkibal via Sopore-Handwara;
(b) whether the proposal has been examined under centrally sponsored schemes such as CRIF, NHIDCL, Bharatmala or others;
(c) the steps being taken to integrate this road with other pending regional link roads and tunnels, prioritisation status and details of actions so far; and
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to declare the Mughal Road as an all-weather National Highway, allocate funds for maintenance and upgradation and ensure smooth connectivity for Poonch, Rajouri, along with the timeframe for permanent solutions?
